  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the equation of hyperbola is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p>As, vertex is at <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;and it passes through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,<br />So,&nbsp;the equation of hyperbola is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>144</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.<br />Equation of normal to the hyperbola at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>y</mi></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Thus, on putting values, equation of normal is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math>.</p>",
